invariant: INV-14
file: quic_token.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the check reads the type byte and ignores it, so a token of the
  reserved NEW_TOKEN type, or of any other, checks as a Retry token whenever
  its tag verifies. RFC 9000 section 8.1.1 requires a server to tell the two
  kinds apart because they need different handling, and the caller reads
  that difference from CH_EPROTO against CH_EAUTH. The type case builds a
  NEW_TOKEN token with a valid tag and requires CH_EPROTO.

--- old
    uint8_t type = rb_u8(&r);
    if (r.err || type != QUIC_TOKEN_TYPE_RETRY) {
--- new
    (void)rb_u8(&r);
    if (r.err) {
